@adampatricknc @haider1 Dude, in the same fireside chat I say that mathematics and coding are two singular exceptions.
The reason is that for those two domains, LLMs can formulate hypotheses and automatically check if they are correct (by running the code or checking the proof).
But that doesn´t work for domains where checking for correctness cannot be done automatically.

